Date: 2α &0 14
EDUCATION AFFILIATION AGREEMENT
Agreement No.EA14-CheyF&R
THIS AGREEMENT, made and entered into as of the date set forth on the
signature page below, by and between Laramie County Community College (hereinafter
referred to as LCCC), whose address is1400East College Drive, CheyenneWY,82007,
andthe City of Cheyenne Fire&Rescue Department(hereinafter referred to as
Provider）whose address is 2101 O'Neil Avenue,3rd Floor, Fire Department
Administration, Cheyenne, WY 82001.LCCC and Provider shall be referred to
individually as“Party”and collectively as“Parties".
WITNESSETH:
WHEREAS, LCCC desires certain services, the scope of which is more fully
described in Articles IV, VandVI and Provider represents and warrants thatit has the
proper licensing, skill and expertise to provide such services;
WHEREAS, LCCC has an established EMT program and offers a degree in the
field ofemergency medical services;
WHEREAS, LCCC desires to provide to its students hands-on education and
learning experiences through the application of knowledge and skills in actual patient-
centered situations; and,
WHEREAS, Provider is willing to provide hands-on education and learning
experiences such situations;
NOW, THEREFORE, The Parties mutually agree to cooperate in the provision of
opportunities for LCCC students to acquire clinical experience in observation and
performance of patient care upon the terms and conditions set forth herein:
I.
DEFINITIONS
A.
"Clinical Experience”means a program of study as part of LCCC's course
or degree requirements, conducted in cooperation with the Provider, whereby students
receive supervised experience and instruction in a professional setting under the direct
supervision of a qualified clinical instructor.Clinical Experience shallbe the same as
clinical training.Nothing in this definition shall be construed or interpreted to waive the
Provider's governmental immunity or to alter, amend, modify or expand the extent to
which the Provider maybe subjected to liability for any of its operations under law.
B.“Site Supervisor” means that person qualified, employed or retained by
the Provider as responsible for the development and administration of the Clinical
Experience affiliation with LCC C, jointly approved by both Parties.
C.
“Student”means aperson enrolled throughLCCC whois toperform the
Clinical Experience and registered in the appropriate certification or degree program.
